Ray Swartz's notes:3dfx RAVE driver Release Notes:Change log (most recent first):15 Aug 00 	1.1d3. Added a NOIDLE flag to the image buffer initialize callback grLfbLock.			Water Race demo now goes 18% faster.04 Aug 00	1.1d2. Reduced memory use by reducing size of alpha states array, after running tests			on Bugdom, Nanosaur, Water Race demo, & Terrain Builder. Optimized SetRenderState by			moving if test to a higher level. Completed RvEngineDeviceCheck for better multimonitor			support. Stopped resetting state flags every frame, speed increase. Utilize more 			memory for textures in non-fullscreen case. Began using compiler option for AltiVec target.03 Aug 00	Enabled use of grTexMaxAddress in case of fullscreen mode; seems			to work now, and this gives us max use of available texture memory.			swapBuffers now supported in fullscreen mode. Optimized treatment of 			1555 textures; no longer cached, speed gain.27 Jul 00 	First change since RC1. 			EngineDeviceCheck now looks at color depth of device. Needs to be 16 or 32.			Still needs work.15 Jul 00	1.0b13d20. Fixed bug in restore state after drawing bitmaps.			Fullscreen mode callbacks fixed. 832x624 mode disallowed in fullscreen.14 Jul 00	Fullscreen mode working. Performance improved 340% in WR Demo.13 Jul 00	Callbacks now stored per context.12 Jul 00	1.0b13d19. Model Builder now working with 5 draw contexts, but			3D World still crashes. Removed vertex buffers for			trimesh, because the driver is faster without them, counterintuitively.			Fixed a restore-state problem in DrawBitmap, which makes Leah look right			in the intro to Water Race.07 Jul 00	Made CalcFogNone not even called if no fog. Eliminated			some unnecessary state-setting. Gestalt now advertises 			AccessDrawBuffer & AccessZBuffer. Renamed functions whose names			started with "glr" or "tnsl". They now start with "Rv" (RAVE).			RvFlush now calls grFlush, rather than grFinish.06 Jul 00	1.0b13d18. Made all SetVertex* functions inlined. r3Vertex.c			is now empty and can be removed from the project.			Removed hardwired "Voodoo5 RAVE" engine name. Maybe the ROM			works right now.05 Jul 00	1.0b13d17. Finished API functions			tnslAccessDrawBuffer(), tnslAccessDrawBufferEnd(),			tnslAccessZBuffer(), tnslAccessZBufferEnd().03 Jul 00	1.0b13d16. Added support for kQAMethod_ReloadTextures callback.			Detects Dark Vengeance and changes default for alpha sorting for			performance.02 Jul 00	1.0b13d15. Moved the calc of usingVertexAlpha to outside the loops.			Several speed optimizations regarding avoiding unneeded setting			of state. Current texture surface allocation is to take the 			total VRAM minus the calculated amt used for back and aux 			buffers minus a 2 MB safety. Then take 13/16 of that. This is			kinda weird and wastes about 6 MB, but it errs on the side of			stability.			Had to hardwire the engine ASCII name as "Voodoo5 RAVE", because			grGetString() was too often returning "ERROR". This will be a			mistake for Voodoo3 & Voodoo5.01 Jul 00	SetBaseTextureFilter enhanced to consider the best of the rave &			opengl settings.29 Jun 00	1.0b13d14. Fixed colorTables. We were passing a pointer to a TQAColorTable to 			grTexDownloadTable, instead of TQAColorTable->pixelData. Now, Kawasaki ATV			support is complete. And the Quake startup screen looks good.28 Jun 00	Provided special handling of Alpha1 textures. This fixed text in Combat Mission.			Fixed calc of bFullScreen, preparing to support Glide fullscreen mode.27 Jun 00	1.0b13d12. In RenderStart, added calls to grSurfaceSetTextureSurface 			any time we're rendering to a new glide context. This is to cover the 			situation where the texture surface was created after the context.			Multiple contexts now work in Terrain Builder, but not in Gerbils. 			3 of 5 Water Race locations work.26 Jun 00	32-bit textures are now converted to 32-bit textures, if Napalm.			Removed the stuff about SetupGlideContext, because it didn't work.24 Jun 00	Fixed a bug where the second time the gestalt for			ASCII name was called, it didn't get the same answer.			In kQAMethod_ImageBufferInitialize, the z-buffer is cleared even			if the context is marked kQAContext_NoZBuffer. This seemed to help			the French-Touch stuff.			Changed SetupGlideContext to be called once at startup, not each 			time a ctx is created. Made some mods to tnslInitialize.23 Jun 00	Commented out CONVERT_NORMAL_W(gv, v); in SetVertex_GouraudSingle,			after seeing it lacking in SetVertex_GouraudThree. 			Got rid of some old logic that associated contexts with texture			surfaces.23 Jun 00	1.0b13d10. Found a missing break stmt in tnslDrawVTexture. 			This fixed some bugs in Combat Mission.			Engine ASCII identifier removes "(tm)" substring and replaces it			with "RAVE". So now, the engine appears in a menu as "Voodoo5 RAVE".21 Jun 00	Changed z-buffer-surface initialization to always use 4 bytes per			pixel when in 32-bit rendering. Ignores RAVE context flag to use			16-bit z-buffer. Previous to this change, only the left half of the			screen was cleared properly.20 Jun 00	Removed "(" from the engine name ID ("Voodoo5 (tm)"), because			this is a special char that tells the Menu Manager that it is a			disabled item.19 Jun 00	1.0b13d9. Supports Nightfall. Needed a custom stw multiplier of 0.0001.19 Jun 00	1.0b13d8. Fixed a z-buffer problem in 32-bits.19 Jun 00	1.0b13d7. 8-bit draw contexts disallowed.			Initialization modified to fix a crash when no hardware found.17 Jun 00	1.0b13d6. Enhanced SetTextureMode to set alpha test values. This 			fixed problems in Kawasaki and Combat Mission.15 Jun 00	1.0b13d5. Removed changes of 13-Jun for stability. Now, Napalm			contexts get a maximum of 15 MB texture memory.13 Jun 00	Created a custom definition for cached Glide state.			We no longer rely on grGlideGetState & grGlideSetState. Saves			116K bytes per context and runs faster. 8 Jun 00	1.0b13d4. Commented out ImageBufferInitialize handling. 			Fixed swimming textures problem by having a special factor  			applied to s,t,w which depends on QD3D vs RAVE. 7 Jun 00	Added macro NAPALM_AND_BEYOND which now controls the 565 hack 			triangles in RenderStart & RenderEnd. 			Now uses hardware when screen is in 8-bit color. 5 Jun 00	Support for bitmaps of any size. For Voodoo3, large bitmaps are 			divided into powers-of-two textures. 3 May 00	Returning ATI gestalt if Quake running. Now, we get a ZSorted_Hint that turns 			off alpha tri cache, greatly reducing dynamic memory use. 2 May 00	Logic for determining if we are caching triangles now takes into account 			whether z func is None. 1 May 00	Gestalt for driver ID no longer reports "3dfx VSA-100". Instead, it uses 			grGetString to return the imbedded string, such as "Voodoo3 (tm)".14 Apr 00	Beta 12. First release of Voodoo3 RAVE. Limited to running 			Bugdom & Nanosaur. Not optimized for speed. Limited to one draw			context. No multitexturing. No specular highlights. No bitmap support.			Some stability problems, probably due to using temporary memory with			locked handles.